{"nodes": [{"id": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_ros_custom_handlers_chrono_ros_handler", "label": "ChROSHandler", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/manuals/ros/custom_handlers.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A handler is the single abstraction that encapsulates all ROS entities (publishers, subscribers, services) and converts messages between ROS and Chrono; all ROS-interacting logic is required to live inside one so ROS concerns stay contained. A complete handler spans four files across two processes."}, {"id": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_ros_custom_handlers_two_process_architecture", "label": "Two-Process Architecture", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/manuals/ros/custom_handlers.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The Chrono simulation process contains NO ROS symbols and the ROS node subprocess contains NO Chrono physics symbols, to guarantee separation and avoid symbol conflicts (particularly between VSG visualization and ROS 2 libraries as of Chrono 9.0). Data crosses as raw serialized bytes over IPC."}, {"id": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_ros_custom_handlers_ipc_shared_header", "label": "Shared IPC Header (*_ipc.h)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/manuals/ros/custom_handlers.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The most critical file: it defines the contract between the two processes. Restricted to plain-old-data structs with no pointers, no std::string/std::vector or other dynamic containers, and no ROS or Chrono headers, so the byte layout is identical and memcpy-serializable on both sides."}, {"id": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_ros_custom_handlers_messagetype_enum", "label": "IPC MessageType Enum", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/manuals/ros/custom_handlers.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Each handler gets a unique MessageType id in src/chrono_ros/ipc/ChROSIPCMessage.h so the subprocess can dispatch an incoming byte stream to the correct registered callback."}, {"id": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_ros_custom_handlers_handler_registry_macro", "label": "CHRONO_ROS_REGISTER_HANDLER", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/manuals/ros/custom_handlers.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Static registration macro binding a MessageType to a subprocess callback. It only runs if the _ros.cpp file is compiled into the chrono_ros_node target; forgetting the CMake step compiles cleanly but produces 'No handler registered for message type' warnings at runtime."}, {"id": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_ros_custom_handlers_chrono_ros_node_target", "label": "chrono_ros_node Executable Target", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/manuals/ros/custom_handlers.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The ROS-side publish/subscribe logic must be compiled into this separate executable rather than the main Chrono library, which is what keeps ROS symbols out of the simulation process."}, {"id": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_ros_custom_handlers_publisher_pattern", "label": "Publisher Pattern (Chrono to ROS)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/manuals/ros/custom_handlers.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Used for sensors and state reporting: the main process extracts and memcpy-serializes into the IPC struct, and the subprocess deserializes and lazily creates a rclcpp publisher held in a static map keyed by topic so it persists across callbacks."}, {"id": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_ros_custom_handlers_subscriber_pattern", "label": "Subscriber Pattern (ROS to Chrono)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/manuals/ros/custom_handlers.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Bidirectional flow for control inputs: a one-time SETUP message carries the topic name from main process to subprocess to trigger subscriber creation, then the subprocess sends received ROS data back over the IPC channel for the main process to apply to Chrono objects."}, {"id": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_ros_custom_handlers_getserializeddata", "label": "ChROSHandler::GetSerializedData", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/manuals/ros/custom_handlers.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_ros_custom_handlers_handleincomingmessage", "label": "ChROSHandler::HandleIncomingMessage", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/manuals/ros/custom_handlers.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Called from the main thread; paired with SupportsIncomingMessages() returning true to enable bidirectional handlers. Chrono object modifications inside it must be made thread-safe when multi-threaded stepping is in use."}, {"id": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_ros_custom_handlers_chrosmanager_registerhandler", "label": "ChROSManager::RegisterHandler", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/manuals/ros/custom_handlers.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The manager is deliberately generic: it calls GetSerializedData() on every registered handler each update and needs no modification for new handler classes, as long as they inherit ChROSHandler."}, {"id": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_ros_custom_handlers_throttling_best_practice", "label": "Handler Throttling", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/manuals/ros/custom_handlers.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Rate limiting inside GetSerializedData (returning an empty vector when it is not yet time) eases stress on ROS and its DDS middleware, because simulation can run many times faster than realtime. A reused member m_buffer avoids per-step vector reallocation."}, {"id": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_ros_custom_handlers_chroscamerahandler", "label": "ChROSCameraHandler", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/manuals/ros/custom_handlers.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Cited as the reference example for complex variable-size data (images), where pixel data follows immediately after the fixed CameraData struct in the byte stream."}, {"id": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_ros_custom_handlers_chrosdriverinputshandler", "label": "ChROSDriverInputsHandler", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/manuals/ros/custom_handlers.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Cited as the reference example for bidirectional control handlers."}, {"id": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_ros_custom_handlers_chmoduleros_swig", "label": "ChModuleROS.i SWIG Interface", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/manuals/ros/custom_handlers.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Optional step: a custom handler must be added to the SWIG interface (header include, %shared_ptr declaration, %include) before it is usable from PyChrono, because SWIG needs the C++ class declaration to generate the wrapper."}], "edges": [{"source": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_ros_custom_handlers_two_process_architecture", "target": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_ros_custom_handlers_chrono_ros_handler", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/manuals/ros/custom_handlers.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_ros_custom_handlers_chrono_ros_handler", "target": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_ros_custom_handlers_ipc_shared_header", "relation": "shares_data_with", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/manuals/ros/custom_handlers.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_ros_custom_handlers_chrono_ros_handler", "target": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_ros_custom_handlers_getserializeddata", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/manuals/ros/custom_handlers.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_ros_custom_handlers_chrono_ros_handler", "target": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_ros_custom_handlers_handleincomingmessage", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/manuals/ros/custom_handlers.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_ros_custom_handlers_getserializeddata", "target": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_ros_custom_handlers_ipc_shared_header", "relation": "shares_data_with", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/manuals/ros/custom_handlers.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "